WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.150
A limited sneaker release.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.910
The line wraps around the block,

3
00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.420
and the shoes sell out in minutes.

4
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.420
Within hours, pairs show
up for resale at well

5
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.310
above the original price.

6
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.990
Across the mall, a store
is stuck with racks

7
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.290
of last season's jackets
that nobody is buying.

8
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.950
One price was too low,

9
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.800
the other too high.

10
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.770
So what pulls a price back to
where buyers and sellers agree?

11
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:28.220
In this mission, you'll find the
price where the market clears,

12
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.570
and calculate the surplus
or shortage when it doesn't.

13
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.790
Then you'll set the
price yourself in a graph

14
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.480
lab and see what happens to the gap.

15
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.520
Your mission: find out
what pulls a price back

16
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.480
to where buyers and sellers agree.
